WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Hi, I'm Chen Xiazi.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Grandma just watered the flowers.
The dirt near the roots looks darker.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The dirt by the path looks lighter.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The little girl crouches by the path.
Dry dirt near her shoes is yellowish-brown.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Wet dirt by the roots is deep brown.
A pale gray stone sits in between.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The colors are right next to each other,
but they look so different.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Grandma scoops dry dirt from the same spot
into two white dishes.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:22.000
The little girl spreads it into two even piles.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:36.000
She drips a few drops of water into the right dish.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:50.000
The wet dirt looks darker.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Now let's mix the first color.
Get white paper, a brush, and washable paint.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Start with a little yellow-ochre,
add a tiny bit of brown and white.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Next, the wet-dirt color.
Darken part of the light mix with more brown.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:20.000
The third stroke is for the little stone.
Add a tiny bit of black to white for pale gray.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Turn it into a small patch of ground.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Paint a big area of light yellowish-brown,
then a patch of deep brown near the roots.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:35.000
The little girl sits by the door
and shows Grandma her painting.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:05:00.000
The darkest color came from the dirt she just watered.
